From: Vishal Ram K N <vishalramkn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 21:24:51 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 126/197] Sketcher: Explain why fillet/chamfer vertex selection
 is blocked for curves

Fixes #24562
---
 src/Mod/Sketcher/Gui/DrawSketchHandlerFillet.h | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Mod/Sketcher/Gui/DrawSketchHandlerFillet.h b/src/Mod/Sketcher/Gui/DrawSketchHandlerFillet.h
index 2ca6d075a..c0d568621 100644
--- a/src/Mod/Sketcher/Gui/DrawSketchHandlerFillet.h
+++ b/src/Mod/Sketcher/Gui/DrawSketchHandlerFillet.h
@@ -80,6 +80,10 @@ public:
                 if (geom1->is<Part::GeomLineSegment>() && geom2->is<Part::GeomLineSegment>()) {
                     return true;
                 }
+                notAllowedReason = QT_TR_NOOP(
+                    "Fillet/chamfer on a point only works between two lines. "
+                    "To fillet curves, select the two edges instead."
+                );
                 // TODO: This could return true for any curve as long as
                 // int SketchObject::fillet(int GeoId, PointPos PosId, double radius, bool trim,
                 // bool createCorner, bool chamfer) evaluates two correct points that can be bound
